@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] shared-kit-fonts-preserve-selection
Both hosts MUST load the checked-in Geist, Mona Sans and code font files for their
named font choices. Unknown saved app or code font choices MUST retain their existing
Geist and Geist Mono fallbacks, and the system choices MUST use the platform's system
families. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, the same app on iOS except for native behavior;
DESIGN.md Typography and N10 (recording 16 Oct 12:10, 06:29 to 06:42).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-kit-web-messages
Android and iOS MUST use the same message lookup, interpolation, plural selection,
offered locales and device-language mapping. Hosts MUST load the web's checked-in
locale JSON through native resource adapters; missing or malformed locale files MUST
fall back to English, and a missing English key MUST remain visible as its key.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS reuse decision; DESIGN.md rule 106 and its web
enforcement. The existing Android message behavior is retained.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion;product] shared-kit-status-marks-reduce-motion
When the native system requests reduced motion, the shared Orb and BreathingDot MUST
hold still, and the Orb's settled-state change and ProgressRing count change MUST
finish immediately. With motion enabled, their existing timings and the Orb's
finish-the-current-turn behavior MUST remain intact. Source: DESIGN.md rules 72, 73
and 97, applied to the shared status marks by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS reuse decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] shared-kit-press-is-only-a-tint
Pressing a row or tile MUST show the existing flat active tint without a ripple,
scale or position change on either host. Source: DESIGN.md rule 82 and F71, retained
by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared-kit decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] shared-kit-both-palettes
Every palette token MUST have light and dark values. Dark surfaces MUST remain neutral
grey as specified by DESIGN.md rule 76 and F13; sharing the kit MUST NOT introduce
platform-specific palette values. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS reuse decision and
DESIGN.md rule 76.
